            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>This SOP applies to operations teams running ads on Meta (Facebook), Google, TikTok, Pinterest, and other platforms for overseas markets. Perform a full compliance audit before launching new campaigns, before major promotions, and during quarterly reviews.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Prepare Before the Audit</h2>
<p>Before starting compliance checks, ensure the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Enable notification channels</strong>: Confirm that your ad account is linked to a valid email and phone number to receive platform risk alerts and violation notices.</li>
<li><strong>Organize your campaign inventory</strong>: List all active campaigns, ad sets, and ads, categorized by platform and region.</li>
<li><strong>Prepare your browser</strong>: Use a clean, incognito mode browser without extensions to avoid triggering security flags from third-party plugins.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Daily Audit (Run Each Day)</h2>
<h3>2.1 Check the Notification Center</h3>
<p>After logging into your ad account, immediately visit the "Notifications" or "Account Quality" page to review any new violation warnings or audit feedback.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Check</strong>: Have all today's notifications been read? Are there any unresolved violation appeals?</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.2 Review Ad Status</h3>
<p>Go through each active ad and watch for these three statuses:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Status</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Paused</td>
<td>Ad is not running</td>
<td>Confirm if paused manually or by the system</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Under Review</td>
<td>Awaiting platform review</td>
<td>Wait 1-24 hours; check if delayed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Disapproved</td>
<td>Policy violation</td>
<td>Review the reason, adjust creative/copy, and resubmit</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>2.3 Monitor Spend Anomalies</h3>
<p>If spend suddenly drops or hits zero, a risk control trigger may have been activated. Investigate promptly:</p>
<ul>
<li>Has the daily budget cap been reached?</li>
<li>Did insufficient balance cause the pause?</li>
<li>Has a policy violation triggered a delivery restriction?</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Weekly Audit (Run Every Monday)</h2>
<h3>Checklist A: Creative Compliance</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Item</th>
<th>Standard</th>
<th>Common Issues</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Text overlay ratio</td>
<td>Text under 20% of image area (Meta policy)</td>
<td>Overloaded promotional text</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Before/after images</td>
<td>Must include "Results may vary" disclaimer</td>
<td>Exaggerated transformations</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Human imagery</td>
<td>No unauthorized celebrities or influencers</td>
<td>Used copyrighted material</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Promotional copy</td>
<td>Avoid absolute claims (e.g., "cheapest ever")</td>
<td>False limited-time offers</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Checklist B: Audience Targeting Compliance</h3>
<ul>
<li>Targeting must not include protected characteristics (race, religion, sexual orientation, etc.).</li>
<li>Certain categories (alcohol, gambling) cannot target users below a specific age threshold.</li>
<li>For finance, education, and health ads, verify that the category is allowed in the target region.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Checklist C: Landing Page Compliance</h3>
<ul>
<li>Does the landing page include a clear link to the privacy policy?</li>
<li>Are data collection forms present with clear usage disclosures?</li>
<li>Does the site support the target region's language and payment methods?</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Common Violations and Responses</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Violation Type</th>
<th>Typical Signs</th>
<th>Urgent Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Misleading claims</td>
<td>Exaggerated efficacy, fake discounts</td>
<td>Pause the ad immediately, revise creative</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Sensitive content</td>
<td>Political or controversial topics</td>
<td>Remove related materials, review copy</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Infringing content</td>
<td>Unauthorized music, logos</td>
<td>Replace with original or licensed assets</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Privacy breaches</td>
<td>No data collection disclosure</td>
<td>Update privacy policy, add statements</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Quick Compliance Checklist (Printable)</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] All today's notifications reviewed</li>
<li>[ ] No unresolved violation warnings</li>
<li>[ ] All active ads are running normally (not paused or disapproved)</li>
<li>[ ] Creative copy contains no exaggerated claims</li>
<li>[ ] Audience targeting excludes protected characteristics</li>
<li>[ ] Landing page includes privacy policy link</li>
<li>[ ] Account balance is sufficient</li>
<li>[ ] Spend anomaly alerts are enabled</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How long should I wait after a disapproval to resubmit?</strong></p>
<p>A: You can resubmit immediately after revising your creative. Platforms typically complete review within 24 hours. If disapproved repeatedly, consider waiting 24 hours before resubmitting.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What should I do after receiving an account restriction notice?</strong></p>
<p>A: First, check the restriction type (spending limit or permanent ban). For temporary restrictions, submit an appeal with required materials. For permanent bans, try submitting business registration documents through official channels for reconsideration.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How do I manage compliance across multiple accounts?</strong></p>
<p>A: Use an ad management tool to centralize notifications and ad statuses across all accounts. Set a unified audit schedule to avoid missing compliance issues.</p>
